00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.070
- My name is Winston Miranda

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:04.960
from Saraba Garifuna Cuisine.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:07.290
My food is typically from my mom's culture

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:08.600
which is the Garifuna people.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.790
My ancestors, they came
from a part of South Africa,

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:13.090
Sierra Leone, and they
migrated to Saint Vincent.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:14.880
And from Saint Vincent
they went to Honduras,

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.710
from Honduras they went to Belize.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:18.190
Our food is very unique.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:20.490
We have one that we call the hudut,

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:22.290
which is like a staple food that

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.820
we eat every day.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:25.040
The fisherman will go to the sea

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:26.270
and bring the fish in,

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:29.070
and then we fry it, we'll
season the coconut milk

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:30.430
and get a flavor off of it,

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:33.520
and add the fish to it,
and boil some plantain.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:34.570
And then they will mash it

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.010
so you can get it real smooth,

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:37.350
and put it like a ball,

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.730
and then you'll eat it
with the coconut milk.

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:42.320
The panades is like a appetizer.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:45.240
Most Americans call it
like, American Hot Pockets.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.750
And it can be eaten any time of the day,

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.420
early in the morning,
late at night, mid-day.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:52.300
We take the masa, and
then we use the achiote.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.530
In Belize they call it
recado, it's a red paste.

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:56.980
And the masa will turn from white to red.

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:57.813
And then people will say,

00:01:57.813 --> 00:01:59.140
"Oh yeah, he's making authentic panades."

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:00.800
Just by the color when people look at it.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.320
You can do it with fish,
you can do it with chicken,

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:04.850
and you can do it with beans.

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:07.143
Flatten it up, and then we fry it.

00:02:07.143 --> 00:02:09.350
There's a habanero onion sauce.

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:11.870
I can make it spicy and
I can make it non-spicy.

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:13.710
Late at night when I'm doing like clubs

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:15.420
and all that stuff, people are drunk,

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.360
so they want the hot, hot one,

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:18.790
the hot habanero sauce.

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:20.480
So, that'll wake them up.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.400
Saraba means "wake up".

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:23.233
- [Andrew] Oh.

00:02:23.233 --> 00:02:24.066
- Yeah.

00:02:24.066 --> 00:02:25.799
