00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:38.410
we're visiting Natalia at WOODSPOON

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:41.260
to try her Brazilian chicken pot pie.

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:45.310
We're also going to have
their house-made sangria.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:48.393
(lighthearted music)

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:53.360
- WOODSPOON serve a traditional
food from Minas Gerais,

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:55.160
where I'm from.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:58.550
We have a lot to offer
in terms of our culinary.

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:01.530
We are very simple, but
our flavor very unique.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:03.370
I was born and raised in Brazil.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:05.590
When I got here, of course,
it was very hard for me

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:08.740
because not speak any English at all.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.940
You know, I didn't understand
why you go to the beach

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:12.500
with an outfit on, you know?

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:14.390
Why can't you get on a bus in a bikini?

00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:17.280
Why you don't go and get
fresh eggs from somewhere,

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:19.480
or there was fresh
chicken from some places.

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:20.790
The way we would do in Brazil

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.170
is a little different than here,

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:23.910
because you have the privilege to buy

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:25.700
just a particular type of meat.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:27.530
There my mom would make a whole chicken.

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:30.490
Here, I was able to buy chicken thigh.

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:32.310
We have to clean them one by one,

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:36.090
removing all the fats,
unnecessary pieces that is there

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:37.370
to make sure it's nice and clean.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:41.560
I save the broth and I use
the fat that stays above

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:42.600
to make the roux.

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:46.090
Add the heart of palm, corn, olives.

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:48.390
A heart of palm is a heart of a palm tree,

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:50.780
and it is a particular one.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:52.630
In Brazil, you can actually get, like,

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:55.720
they can be this tall, this big.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:59.280
But here, we only get the
very small parts of it.

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:01.990
Corn, we had it everywhere in the backyard

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:03.460
where we planted it ourselves.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:05.800
Olives, because you
know, we are Portuguese.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:09.020
Brazil is a country with
all countries in it.

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:11.640
You know, people get surprised how we have

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:13.480
the biggest Japanese
community in the world

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:14.313
is in Brazil.

00:06:14.313 --> 00:06:16.840
There is more Lebanese in
Brazil than in Lebanon.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:20.530
Like, we have in my town
in Minas, a lot of Chinese.

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:22.560
Because the agriculture, the farming.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:25.240
We have stroganoff, a German dish.

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:27.600
We have all these incredible

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:31.110
cultures and gastronomy in Brazil

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:33.230
that I felt like opening WOODSPOON

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:35.450
would give me an opportunity to

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:38.190
show a little bit more
what Brazil can offer.

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:40.830
I just wanted people to know Brazil

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:42.660
not just the postcard,

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:45.200
but also into those little cultures

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:49.020
that it's so rich, and so
real, and so important.

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:50.150
This is my home.

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:51.530
Whatever we can do for people

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:54.270
to educate themselves through food.

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:57.240
I believe food is a bridge
that connects us all,

00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:58.810
and this is mine.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:00.390
- Okay, fellas.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.400
